From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:50:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: say which provider refuses an external
 DCP power-down

On the J604 both external DCPs log "idle: power-down not possible now
(-19)" once at boot, so the idle power-down after dcpext_idle_ms never
runs. The DART, PMC interface and PMGR domain checks are chained with ?:
and the message cannot tell which of them refused.

Run them one at a time and name the one that refused in the warning.
Nothing else changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 9aa1a5ea9c..3441f005c2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -5903,11 +5903,18 @@ static int iomfb_m4_ext_power_gate(struct iomfb_m4 *dcp, const char *why)
 	ret = dcp_m4_runtime_live(r);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	ret = apple_dart_dcp_power_check(dcp->dev) ?:
-	      apple_pmc_interface_consumer_check(dcp->dev) ?:
-	      apple_pmgr_ps_consumer_check(dcp->dev);
+	step = "DART";
+	ret = apple_dart_dcp_power_check(dcp->dev);
+	if (!ret) {
+		step = "PMC interface";
+		ret = apple_pmc_interface_consumer_check(dcp->dev);
+	}
+	if (!ret) {
+		step = "PMGR domains";
+		ret = apple_pmgr_ps_consumer_check(dcp->dev);
+	}
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_warn(dcp->dev, "%s: power-down not possible now (%d)\n", why, ret);
+		dev_warn(dcp->dev, "%s: power-down not possible now: %s (%d)\n", why, step, ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
